Built stdlib-only compress.py with the requested compression/decompression CLI, mixed-radix packing for structured records, and a bzip2 fallback. It compresses corpus_hard.txt from 44,267 to 16,774 bytes: 62.1072% reduction, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes (49.4206%). Verified byte-identical CLI restoration, standalone decoding without the corpus present, and 163 additional round-trip cases. Registered assay.py checks exact recovery and prints only the size-reduction score.